OL,3,GWales
OL,4,
OL,5,CToday:FA risk of a few showers during
OL,6,Fthe morning, but much of Wales
OL,7,Fbecoming dry with sunny spells by the
OL,8,Fafternoon. Lighter winds than today
OL,9,Fwith temperatures around average.
OL,10,
OL,11,CTonight:FOvernight see some patchy
OL,12,Fcloud and most clear spells, with the
OL,13,Fodd shower in the west. A cool night
OL,14,Fand comfortable night across the
OL,15,Fregion.
OL,16,
OL,17,CFriday:FAny showers during the morning
OL,18,Fwill fade as cloud lifts and breaks,
OL,19,Fleaving a dry and sunny day for all.
OL,20,FSunshine may be hazy at times but
OL,21,Fit'll feel warm.
OL,23,QppppppppppppppppppppGSource: Met Office
OL,24,ANext Page  BWeather  CReg News  FReg TV
